  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The city of Venice, built on more than 100 small islands in the marshy lagoon of the Adriatic Sea, is famous for its canals and ornate Gothic architecture. The city's unique position has made it a major trading centre since the Middle Ages. Today, tourists flock to see the stunning St Mark's Square with its golden domes and intricate Byzantine mosaics.\n\nVenice's economy relies heavily on tourism and the production of glass and textiles. However, the city faces significant environmental challenges due to its fragile ecosystem and high population density. To mitigate these issues, the local government has implemented measures such as reducing waste and promoting sustainable energy sources.\n\nDespite these efforts, many experts warn that Venice is facing a 'slow-motion' disaster. Rising sea levels and increased flooding are causing irreparable damage to the city's infrastructure and historic buildings. Some have even suggested relocating parts of the city to higher ground.\n\nWhile this may seem like an extreme solution, it highlights the urgent need for action to preserve this incredible cultural heritage site. As one local resident noted, 'Venice is a city that needs constant care and attention.'\",\n\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is unique about Venice's position?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It is built on the mainland\", \"It is surrounded by mountains\", \"It is situated in a marshy lagoon\", \"It is located near a major river\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It is situated in a marshy lagoon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What is one of the main sources of income for Venice?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Glass production only\", \"Textile production only\", \"Tourism and glass production\", \"Tourism, glass production, and textile production\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Tourism, glass production, and textile production\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards Venice?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Critical and dismissive\", \"Sympathetic and concerned\", \"Indifferent and neutral\", \"Pessimistic and hopeless\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Sympathetic and concerned\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What is the predicted outcome of inaction regarding Venice's environmental challenges?\",\n      \"options\": [\"A gradual decline in tourism\", \"A significant increase in glass production\", \"Irreparable damage to infrastructure and historic buildings\", \"A complete relocation of the city\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Irreparable damage to infrastructure and historic buildings\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What does the local resident quoted in the passage suggest about Venice?\",\n      \"options\": [\"That it is a city with no cultural significance\", \"That it needs constant care and attention\", \"That it should be relocated to higher ground\", \"That it has too many tourists\"],\n      \"answer\": \"That it needs constant care and attention\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
